      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Half a scoop of pre-workout might seem like a safer bet, but it's still playing with fire. Beta alanine can cause tingling and muscle fatigue, and caffeine can spike your heart rate. An extra antihistamine isn't a magic fix either; it could mask symptoms of a more serious reaction. I'd say, take a break from the pre-workout, hydrate, and focus on your lifts. Your body will thank you for it. And remember, no rush—your health is more important than a single gym session.",
      "source": "target",
